/*
 * Azure Batch profile — e.g. launched from Seqera Platform with an Azure Batch compute
 * environment (DTU BRIGHT). Use as `-profile azure`.
 *
 * Under Seqera the compute environment supplies everything site-specific: credentials, the
 * Batch pool, region and the az:// work directory. This profile only sets what the pipeline
 * itself decides, so it holds no account names or secrets and nothing needs editing for a
 * new site. The tool image comes from params.strainqc_container (default: the published
 * image for this release), which Batch nodes pull from ghcr.io.
 *
 * Running WITHOUT Seqera (plain `nextflow run`): also set the account credentials, e.g. via
 * the environment variables AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_NAME / _KEY and AZURE_BATCH_ACCOUNT_NAME /
 * _KEY, plus `-w az://<container>/work` and azure.batch.location. See
 * docs/deploy_seqera_azure.md.
 */

process.executor = 'azurebatch'

// Inputs and reference databases live in Azure Blob storage (az:// paths). Kraken2/MASH
// databases are large: stage them once into the storage account and pass
// --kraken2_db az://.../kraken_db  --mash_db az://.../refseq.msh
//
// Task sizes: base.config labels request up to 8 CPUs / 32 GB, capped by --max_cpus /
// --max_memory. Keep those at or below the largest VM in the Batch pool
// (default 16 CPUs / 64 GB, i.e. a Standard_D16s_v3-class VM).
